{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it","id":19242,"title":"Fae-ify It!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-27T10:07:04-08:00","id":19242,"title":"Fae-ify It!","content":"A thread from the old boards that I think we should start here again. Take something from somewhere else, be it a fictional character, story, place, even a real-life event or person, and add that Changeling twist.<br /> <br /> He doesn't remember his name, and it's not important, because that's not who he is anymore. He vaguely remembers his life before, being a two-bit bankrobber with better ideas than he could execute, but that's not important anymore either. He remembers being on the run from some cops, or maybe other crooks, turning a corner, and finding himself in a deep hedge. And then things got. . . stranger.<br /> <br /> He finally escaped, and he doesn't want to go back. But he remembers the pure, simple beauty of chaos, of the only reality being the one you decided upon at any given instant, and he sees this rigid, structured world and can't help but think that it needs more chaos. He's an agent of chaos.<br /> <br /> He's painted his Mask to reflect his Mein. White makeup on his face, black around his eyes, a red slash of a smile over the scars on his cheeks, and green dye in his hair. When people see beneath the Mask, they see skin bleached whiter than bone, empty black pits for eyes, a bleeding red gash where his mouth should be, and green fire atop his head for hair. He calls himself the Joker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","user":"ErikModi","date":". 03-04-2014, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T09:37:37-08:00","id":84010,"title":"","content":"Its Realm is Pieced together from the dreams of children that ask too many questions, stitched together with crayons and construction paper. from its throne of curiosities and stolen imagination The Monster asks the stolen questions of all that It has Dragged to its lair; The marine biologist that questioned her position as a female in a male dominated field and now swims in a tank of her own tears. Forced every night to endure hellish dreams wrought by a monster that can only pretend to care. The opera singer and his family whos voices were stolen and replaced with honks and squeaks act out the answers to the same questions over and over again, bound in a window near where the Monster sleeps and constantly watched by the Monsters soulless unblinking eyes. there were many more but it has been so long ago that i escaped . . .Elmo's World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1445-elesho","name":"elesho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:52:36-07:00","id":90337,"title":"","content":"Bruce Wayne was born to an extraordinarily rich doctor. After his parent were murdered, he became a distant lad. Only his butler was able to get through to him, but one night, IT CAME. It called itself Azrael and it took the young master Wayne into the dark. There young Bruce was dumped into a dark and twisted cave full of monstrous bats. It took him years to fight off his fear, but when he learned to embrace his fear, he found others in the dark. These others taught him how to fight and survive in the lightless cave. He learned how to track and hunt. He learned to use his mind and body as an instrument, and one day he found his way out of the cave, and back into the alley behind the theatre. <br /> He made his way home, but another was there. Another Bruce living his life. This Bruce was a spoiled slave of desire. Lost in his/its desires. In one swift motion, Bruce killed his doppelganger, and resumed his place as the prodigal son of Wayne Manor. To the outside world Bruce Wayne is still the lost playboy, but to the criminals of Gotham, there is a monster in the dark. A creature that prowls the twisted and dark alleys of the city. This monster has the form of a man, but on certain nights, when the moon casts is baleful light, the monster can be seen beneath the cowl. A monster who feeds off of their terror. A monster known only as the BATMAN!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2506-angelofmurphy","name":"AngelofMurphy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T11:00:36-07:00","id":90342,"title":"","content":"Bruce Banner grew up as most boys do, but unlike most, Bruce was a genius. He graduated high school by the age of nine. By thirteen, he received his first degree. By the time he was in his mid twenties, he was the lead in his field as a physicist with his specialty in radiation.<br /> While working late one night with his fianc\u00e9, Betty, a horrendous monster broke into his lab. It destroyed everything and did its best to kill Bruce. But when Betty fell onto Bruce's broken body in tears, begging for the horrible green monster to stop\u2026it did. It turned and left.<br /> Bruce was in a coma for several days, but when he awoke, he was a changed man. He took a leave of absence of work, and went in search of the green monster. He had a responsibility to it\u2026no to him. When Bruce had looked into the monsters eyes, he had seen the truth; the horrible truth. Bruce was not Bruce Banner. He was just a thing, a fake, a simulacrum made of leaves and moss.<br /> The real Bruce had been stolen as a child by an even greater monster, and beaten and tortured until he had become that monstrous green man. He and Betty would dedicate the rest of their lives to finding this child in the body of a great ogre and they would care for him. They would educate him if they could. They would make him whole again as best they could. Betty would become his mother, and Bruce would do his best as a father.<br /> Bruce Banner had thought he was a good man. But now he knows he is not a man, but he would still be the best he could be\u2026whatever he was. And he WILL teach the real Bruce how to be human again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2506-angelofmurphy","name":"AngelofMurphy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T01:08:13-07:00","id":112476,"title":"","content":"the children skipped merrily into the classroom, though no one dared utter the unspoken truth. one by one they each gave a lesson, one by one they each sang a song for the bloated purple beast eyeing them with a hungry gleam behind its smiling plastic eyes. at night when all the hugs were had and all the songs were sung, the children would sleep doing their best not to cry for those were the ones who...disappeared. and every morning they rose to start the cycle a new, each day a new lesson each day the same songs. each day their spirits would break a little more to the tune of &quot;i love you...you love me...&quot; each day the children would wait for one of their own to cry at night and fall victim to...Barney the purple dinosaur...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T01:44:38-07:00","id":163280,"title":"","content":"It was just supposed to be a Game with a group of friends. You had been waiting patiently for weeks after you heard about a game that was more realistic and immersing than anything you had ever heard of, you and your friend couldn't wait to begin playing it. Sure you all had some difficulty from a few online trolls and their ridiculous &quot;Warning&quot; attempts at trolling but they were easily ignored. Once the game was in your possession you all swiftly learned just how powerful it really was. It took you all away from your lives and forced you all to play a game that mortals were never supposed to play, you saw strange creatures made cobbled together memories from your childhoods, Waring Cities of Lights and Shadows, Strange Monsters that lived beneath the strange worlds the game had created, the end of all things, A Sky that brought Visions in its clouds, Things that should not be behind the walls of reality, a Black Demon made of broken dreams, a Witch Queen from another World, a Green monster that brought Death in its wake, and the strangest of all was finding out the Internet Trolls who were seemingly fucking with you were players who were trying to warn you to not play this horrible game. The Game would Challenge you, Break you, Raise you, and ultimately change you into something much more and far less that what you ever were.<br /> <br /> Envelog:<br /> Glamour response detected.<br /> Glamour accepted.<br /> Grafting to soul.<br /> Connecting to Prospit server.<br /> Dreamself generated.<br /> Connecting to Arcadia server.<br /> Awaiting response from the Noble Lords of Faerie<br /> Noble Lords of Faerie rejected request for rename. Laughed.<br /> Redirecting to Dark Fates Foretold<br /> Connected. Uplink to WYRD established.<br /> Connecting to Skaia server.<br /> Connection established.<br /> Welcome to the Sburb, Jane Crocker, Maid of Life.<br /> Your game pass was provided by: Her Imperious Condescension.<br /> <br /> It was only supposed to be a Game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T02:15:09-07:00","id":163306,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/28VOLdy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I have no words...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T03:34:01-07:00","id":163353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jane_Dargason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=163280#post163280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was only supposed to be a Game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds great, but what's the source?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1969-alexander","name":"Alexander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1969_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T18:29:51-07:00","id":164278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alexander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=163353#post163353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds great, but what's the source?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Homestuck. Webcomic, very, very long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:29:42-07:00","id":165292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its Realm is Pieced together from the dreams of children that ask too many questions, stitched together with crayons and construction paper. from its throne of curiosities and stolen imagination The Monster asks the stolen questions of all that It has Dragged to its lair; The marine biologist that questioned her position as a female in a male dominated field and now swims in a tank of her own tears. Forced every night to endure hellish dreams wrought by a monster that can only pretend to care. The opera singer and his family whos voices were stolen and replaced with honks and squeaks act out the answers to the same questions over and over again, bound in a window near where the Monster sleeps and constantly watched by the Monsters soulless unblinking eyes. there were many more but it has been so long ago that i escaped . . .Elmo's World. </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Now I can study all the night without coffee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T20:35:56-07:00","id":165582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it#post19242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thread from the old boards that I think we should start here again. Take something from somewhere else, be it a fictional character, story, place, even a real-life event or person, and add that Changeling twist.<br /> <br /> He doesn't remember his name, and it's not important, because that's not who he is anymore. He vaguely remembers his life before, being a two-bit bankrobber with better ideas than he could execute, but that's not important anymore either. He remembers being on the run from some cops, or maybe other crooks, turning a corner, and finding himself in a deep hedge. And then things got. . . stranger.<br /> <br /> He finally escaped, and he doesn't want to go back. But he remembers the pure, simple beauty of chaos, of the only reality being the one you decided upon at any given instant, and he sees this rigid, structured world and can't help but think that it needs more chaos. He's an agent of chaos.<br /> <br /> He's painted his Mask to reflect his Mein. White makeup on his face, black around his eyes, a red slash of a smile over the scars on his cheeks, and green dye in his hair. When people see beneath the Mask, they see skin bleached whiter than bone, empty black pits for eyes, a bleeding red gash where his mouth should be, and green fire atop his head for hair. He calls himself the Joker.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Why so serious?&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://skottieyoung.deviantart.com/art/Joker-Commission-173064876\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://fc04.deviantart.net/fs71/f/2010/209/b/a/Joker_Commission_by_skottieyoung.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:34:59-07:00","id":166128,"title":"","content":"There were a couple of mine from the old thread that I'm still pretty proud of...<br /> <br /> ~~The last thing Peter Parker could remember was the spider's bite... or was it the prick of a thorn on the back of his hand? His next recollections were of a dark, dreamlike existence of a tangled silken maze that he learned to navigate as naturally as walking across the ground, constantly wary of danger. When a stranger passed by his web, Peter paid him no mind, but the sight of the passage the stranger took stirred vague memories in the little spider. His Aunt and Uncle must be worried about him.<br /> <br /> Deftly skittering along the bramble-strewn path, he blinked all of his eyes in confusion at several bright, flashing lights as he emerged. Police. He remembered police. And there was a body on the ground, there. Horrified, he recognized his Uncle Ben. A stranger had approached him from the darkness, witnesses said, and fled after the old man fell before him. Acting on instinct, Peter gave chase after the fleeing murderer over walls and rooftops before finally catching up to the fiend who murdered his beloved Uncle. But when he saw the man's face, he received a terrible shock.<br /> <br /> Uncle Ben had indeed worried about his lost nephew when he hadn't come home, and went searching for him. Instead, he encountered the thing that had passed by Peter's web, sent to take his place. Startled, the fetch had lashed out and killed Uncle Ben, taking flight when it realized its mistake. Peter watched in horror as the thing with his face dissolved into drifting cobwebs in his grasp, then made his way back home to his grieving Aunt May, who was simply relieved that her nephew was back safe and sound.<br /> <br /> Today, Peter has resumed his mortal life, but he's also sworn himself to the Spring Court of the Manhattan Freehold, supplementing his doting Aunt May's wages as a freelance photographer. Using his spiderlike gifts to dazzle and amaze his fellow Changelings with acts of daring gymnastics and acrobatics, he laughs in the face of danger as he evades and taunts the varied privateers that threaten the Freehold with spectacular wit and agility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:51:04-07:00","id":166142,"title":"","content":"And another:<br /> <br /> ~~It is said that the Tainted Coil was the first of the Others to cross out of Arcadia and claim subjects for itself, twisting and changing them according to its sick and warped desires until they no longer had any memory of their past lives and former beautiful forms. Ormagodden, the Cremator of the Skies was brought low by the song of a lovely Fairest named Etulia, and the Tainted Coil slew him, rending his steel flesh so that its changeling children would never have to bear the pain of seeing each other's new forms by his burning light. But the rage, fire and steel unleashed in the Fire Beast's death cry laid the foundations of rebellion and drive for freedom in every changeling to come. The Tainted Coil and its Changeling slaves remain in Arcadia to this day, as does Etulia, eternally weeping a sea of black tears at the loss of Ormagodden and the hole left in her heart by the role she played in the Tainted Coil's betrayal. Her black tears bring power to those who drink it, but also madness.<br /> <br /> Ages have passed in both Arcadia and the mortal realm, but time twists upon itself in Arcadia. And so, long ages after his death at the hands of the Tainted Coil, the Fire Beast claimed a mortal roadie named Eddie Riggs and spirited him back to the realm of the Fae. There he brought knowledge of how to use Ormagodden's gifts to help rekindle the fires of rebellion in the Changelings living under the oppression of the Tainted Coil's loyalist General, the decadent and cruel Lionwhyte. With a handful of free-thinking Changelings, they established the freehold of Bladehenge and began their push against the forces that stand between them, the Hedge, and freedom. For Ormagodden saw that Eddie had a great destiny, written in the pledges forged by his ensorcelled mortal father and upon the death of his mother...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T11:59:51-07:00","id":167123,"title":"","content":"Officer Ronald Frashour in the Portland Police Bureau of Portland Oregon has sprayed a woman in the face with pepperspray during a domestic disturbance call while she was fleeing him to her own bathroom, tasered unarmed citizens without warning and shot from behind an unarmed grieving man to death with his police rifle but fate decrees that he shall remain a police officer until he breaks his pledge to keep and enforce the secrets of Portland's Autumn Monarch. Fear of police brutality, and violence in general keeps Portland peaceful, which is the way the Freehold Monarch of Soggy Stumptown like it. The police are terrified of their suspects and react with disproportionate force, sometimes lethally, to avoid the potential for injury. This has the side effect of keeping the summer court weak because overt anger and violence are not accepted within Portland. (Real life events)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T09:09:53-07:00","id":289641,"title":"","content":"The town itself is nothing special. A tiny rural settlement hours away by car or train, one example in a million of a sleepy village whose industry is slowly being robbed by a large department store dominating local markets and driving the old shopping district out of business. All that really matters is that it is a small place where everyone knows one another. The perfect place for the Lady of Mist and Rain to begin her game. It begins simply enough. The Hedge fills with a thick fog, making it impossible to see the thorns. Sometimes the fog drifts into the real world. The Lady crosses into the world herself at times, often when it rains. She tells a rumor of the Midnight Channel, an image that appears on a TV screen in the town at midnight (at the precise moment when yesterday becomes today). She draws on the dreams of the town to weave the visions seen. Time passes, the rumors spread. Finally, she crafts an especially wide Trod with an odd key. A changeling that has accepted its fetch and become one can enter this trod through a television inside the town. The trod leads to a strange otherplace, a hollow crafted purely from the hidden dreams of those that walk the trod. But the truth is grim- the Lady crafts this hollow by abducting any mortals who walk the path. She leaves the fetch in the center of this broken hollow. For the fetch it has been a moment, for the changeling a lifetime. The changeling and fetch are given a moment to accept one another. This is made horribly difficult because the Lady has spent time educating the changeling in everything loathsome and hideous about themselves, letting the vile yellow taint of her fog seep into their eyes. The changelings inevitably spit these lessons of hate back at their often bewildered fetches, who cannot help but reject the harsh truths they are given. A fetch that rejects their counterpart is killed by the fae, their body taken by the Lady into the real world and hung from a telephone pole or antenna. The changeling becomes a goblin, deadly and powerful. When all is ready, the Lady picks her pawns among the strangers who enter the town. She infects their dreams, and births aspects of monsters inside their minds. She names her dream children False Hope, the Mad Messiah, and the Idle Despair. The world falls still, the players are ready to enact their roles, and the curtain rises. The killings have begun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:02:03-07:00","id":293064,"title":"","content":"There is a legend whispered among the changelings in the City of Endless Summer: a Mirrorskin, officially burned by all four Courts under a cloud of suspicion. The rumors range from selling the secrets of one Court to another, to accusations of being a Loyalist. He hasn't been banished, however... no matter what Grandfather Thunder or the other monarchs might wish for him, there are greater, more mysterious forces compelling them to leave him be, for now. In fact, this conspiracy seems very concerned with keeping our beleaguered changeling pinned down in Miami and cut off from the aid of the Courts or anyone outside the Freehold.<br /> <br /> Still, not every changeling spurns him. There are always those in need of his special skills and knowledge, who have nowhere else to turn. There are also a few old friends within the Courts willing to lend a hand for a good cause. And so he survives, trading his craft for cash, favors and Glamour, quietly working under cover of suspicion and conspiracy to find whoever's responsible for burning him, so that he can one day fully take back his own life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T01:18:13-08:00","id":374113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=293064#post293064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And so he survives, trading his craft for cash, favors and Glamour, quietly working under cover of suspicion and conspiracy to find whoever's responsible for burning him, so that he can one day fully take back his own life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Michael Westen, right? Is his girlfriend a Fireheart?<br /> -<br /> Deep within the city, there is a Fae who punishes the greed of little girls- and there is <i>so </i>much of it, enough to feed him and his kind for eternity. One girl wants to live through the car crash she's in. Another wants to heal her best friend's disability. And there is a lonely, bitter outcast who would do <i>anything</i> to turn back time.<br /> The Fae gives them all these things, and strange beautiful powers, if they only agree to fight other Fae. It's reasonable, isn't it? Nothing comes free.<br /> So the girls agree, and he kills their human shells- <i>such </i>unreliable, frail things, not good at all for fighting- and gives them new bodies. Changeling bodies, that are strong and aware of the World of Darkness around them.<br /> And because this Fae is so good, he places their souls in shining gems, where his girls can keep them safe. Gems that only break when the Changeling evolves into a Fae.<br /> Of course, he doesn't tell them any of that. It would just upset them.<br /> Humans are so irrational.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T19:45:21-08:00","id":374700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=374113#post374113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michael Westen, right? Is his girlfriend a Fireheart?<br /> -<br /> Deep within the city, there is a Fae who punishes the greed of little girls- and there is <i>so </i>much of it, enough to feed him and his kind for eternity. One girl wants to live through the car crash she's in. Another wants to heal her best friend's disability. And there is a lonely, bitter outcast who would do <i>anything</i> to turn back time.<br /> The Fae gives them all these things, and strange beautiful powers, if they only agree to fight other Fae. It's reasonable, isn't it? Nothing comes free.<br /> So the girls agree, and he kills their human shells- <i>such </i>unreliable, frail things, not good at all for fighting- and gives them new bodies. Changeling bodies, that are strong and aware of the World of Darkness around them.<br /> And because this Fae is so good, he places their souls in shining gems, where his girls can keep them safe. Gems that only break when the Changeling evolves into a Fae.<br /> Of course, he doesn't tell them any of that. It would just upset them.<br /> Humans are so irrational.</div> </div> </div> </div>KYUUBEYYY! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (We need an &quot;angry&quot; emoticon).<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> The Neurosurgeon Knight was sane, once. <br /> <br /> Well, okay, not sane; he always had troubles, such as the idea that animals don't matter when you're learning the ins and outs of their biology. But he was a child, and he wasn't always a sociopath. That was before his sister and he were taken by the Burning Man. The Burning Man the common folk called, because his family was rich and they were not (actually, the Burning Man was just going to burn their family's barn, but then he noticed the two children and decided nobody would mind if he took them with him). He came back. His sister didn't, and it was by her sacrifice that he came back.<br /> <br /> And he came back twisted. He hated humans now, and what he saw of his father's dreams never convinced him to stop hating them. His young scientific genius lost what ethics it had; by the time he murdered his parents, the Knight already had a professional's knowledge of the brain, and by the time the doctor came to him, he possessed an intuitive knowledge that seemed almost divine. The doctor was impressed and scared, both by this mad <i>wunderkind </i>and his even more impressive ability to Skeinwalk. Faking sympathy to his plight, they build a machine together, a way to accomplish through technology what the True Fae could do naturally. Then the doctor betrayed the Knight, and the Knight was stripped of all but his brain and soul, forced into his own machine.<br /> <br /> The doctor was a very foolish man.<br /> <br /> The Knight is not, the Knight anticipated this, and he had long learned how to extend his own dreams into the waking world. Small effects, yes, but enough to send all around him to sleep, draw them into his own dream where he was effectively god and king. He selected a youth, a Cambion, to be the new vessel for his soul, and he overwrote the minds of others to become a legion of Incubi. He grew stronger, strong enough to manifest his own self-image outside the machine and vent his fury on the world that took his sister away and then sealed him within his own invention. And then three police officers, two mortals and a hidden changeling, came to his hospital. <br /> <br /> Three new people were drawn into the dream...<br /> <br /> (I'll be happily surprised if anyone guesses what game this is)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T20:13:27-08:00","id":374755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=374700#post374700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'll be happily surprised if anyone guesses what game this is)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a tale about some resident evil of a <b>ru</b>eful <b>vic</b>tim's mind.<br /> <br /> We don't like to talk about the boy in the box.<br /> <br /> He lives in a shipping container on the roof of the school and he barely attends. Ever since those fatally bizarre incidents started happening around town he's been talking to himself about some really disturbing flights of fancy. Stuff like the government being controlled by a cult to an Demon Lord out of some cheesy light novel, some horsecrap about reality and perception and shape that he probably took out of a cartoon, muttering about how he isn't real\u2026 And then there's all that babbling about the last year's earthquakes, as if we needed that kind of walking panic attack wandering the halls.<br /> <br /> Does he even go to this school? Nobody I know remembers seeing his name on the class register. What was it again\u2026?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T15:02:42-08:00","id":375609,"title":"","content":"It was advertised as a paradise, a place where information flowed freely and you could create nearly anything you could imagine. Here, you could adopt a new persona, and say anything you wanted to whoever you wanted and suffer no repercussions, because there was nothing they could physically do to stop you. It wasn't until you entered this paradise that you encountered the threats it possessed. Armies of Trolls eager to destroy all that was good in the world, and massive wars that brought fire to the land. There were even cases of marauders hacking their way through your land, stealing your finances, spreading disease and taking control over your life. You tried to leave, but discovered you couldn't bring yourself to do it, as you had become entranced by this new world. Every time you tried to leave, your pulse would race and your nerves tingle as you quickly ran back to your safe zone. Here you could be sheltered from the outside world. Here you could be whoever you wanted to be. You learned how to destroy the Troll's food supply, and the fiery wars only continued as long as neither side relented. You even learned how to build a wall to keep the marauders off your territory!<br /> <br /> This is your life now, welcome to the Internet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-19-2015, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T01:12:15-08:00","id":375957,"title":"","content":"Hidden within a forest, there is a rural village guarded by red butterflies. It is pretty and peaceful and quiet- so quiet, indeed, that people there can hear <i>~ </i>whispering.<br /> Hidden within a forest, there is an abandoned ruin, rotting and creaky with age. Sometimes, when darkness falls, and twins step over the boundary line- and <i>only</i> twins- the two become one.<br /> <br /> The past isn't that different from the present, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T13:28:42-08:00","id":376571,"title":"","content":"Young Wade Wilson was never a well adjusted person. His mother died of cancer when he was very young, and his father was abusive. As a teenager, he was a delinquent and was kicked out of the military for bad behavior. After being diagnosed with cancer, he met a group of men who claimed to be from the government and promised to cure his cancer if he accepted to participate in a top secret biological augmentation program. However, these men were actually True Fae in the shape of Grey Aliens, and their experiments turned Wade into a deadly warrior. Wade was driven insane by the experience and refused to obey the commands of the Greys, who deemed him a failure and locked him away with other failed test subjects. He managed to escape from Arcadia with powerful Tokens and an amazing healing factor, but upon seeing that he was considered dead by the world, he snapped for good. He retreated into the Hedge and made more weapons, a Hollow and a Hedgespun suit to hide his deformity that was visible even through the Mask. He turned into a mercenary for hire with a love for bad jokes and chimichangas. His broken memories led him to believe there was some sort of cruel betting game among the failed test subjects, and he decided to give himself the same name: Deadpool.<br /> <br /> (In game terms: Deadpool is a Courtless Ogre, and his kiths are Stonebones/Soldier. He has a special Merit that allows him to spend 1 glamour and roll Wyrd + Stamina, with each success healing one lethal damage or two bashing damage. He heals aggravated wounds like bashing wounds, and when his health meter is filled with aggravated damage, he falls unconscious instead of dying. He has Wyrd 7 and very low Clarity, and killing people is no longer a breaking point for him.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T16:05:41-08:00","id":378445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=374755#post374755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a tale about some resident evil of a <b>ru</b>eful <b>vic</b>tim's mind.<br /> <br /> We don't like to talk about the boy in the box.<br /> <br /> He lives in a shipping container on the roof of the school and he barely attends. Ever since those fatally bizarre incidents started happening around town he's been talking to himself about some really disturbing flights of fancy. Stuff like the government being controlled by a cult to an Demon Lord out of some cheesy light novel, some horsecrap about reality and perception and shape that he probably took out of a cartoon, muttering about how he isn't real\u2026 And then there's all that babbling about the last year's earthquakes, as if we needed that kind of walking panic attack wandering the halls.<br /> <br /> Does he even go to this school? Nobody I know remembers seeing his name on the class register. What was it again\u2026?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Where does this come from?<br /> <br /> Honestly sounds interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T18:23:52-08:00","id":378564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=378445#post378445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...Where does this come from?<br /> <br /> Honestly sounds interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from <i>Ch\u00e4os;Head</i>, mostly drawing from the fact that the story establishes early on how <i>utterly disconnected from reality</i> the protagonist is.<br /> <br /> It helps that hallucinations are a recurring plot element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T16:52:03-08:00","id":379632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=375957#post375957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hidden within a forest, there is a rural village guarded by red butterflies. It is pretty and peaceful and quiet- so quiet, indeed, that people there can hear <i>~ </i>whispering.<br /> Hidden within a forest, there is an abandoned ruin, rotting and creaky with age. Sometimes, when darkness falls, and twins step over the boundary line- and <i>only</i> twins- the two become one.<br /> <br /> The past isn't that different from the present, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Didn't we promise...we'd always be together? Together...forever...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T20:48:07-08:00","id":379787,"title":"","content":"Wow. . . really glad to see this thread finally taking off! Some GREAT ideas here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T21:16:54-08:00","id":386987,"title":"","content":"Your family is gone. They disappeared into the sky, drawn by a nameless force- like dust in a whirlwind.<br /> In your loneliness, you hear the Call. The Call that urges you to <i>descend</i>, to dive through wave and reef and cave until you have found them.<br /> You swim so long and so far you forget what you were. Your tongue remembers only the taste of raw fish. Your voice sings songs no human could ever compose. You breathe less and less.<br /> ...And one day- the day you find It- you realize you no longer need to breathe at all.<br /> <br /> Yet, no matter what you turn into, one sign of your identity remains.<br /> The marks on your head...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T21:25:35-08:00","id":402965,"title":"","content":"There was once an African prince, a gold-cloaked boy who owned everything under the sun. It seemed his life would be happy- so happy, in fact, that the prince's uncle grew envious. He plotted murder, but had not the courage to carry out his ambitions...<br /> ...not until a band of scavengers, dark-spotted and scrawny, approached him and offered allegiance. They had come from a shadowed land, a place on no map, and were hungry for life. With them as his pawns, the traitor felt emboldened.<br /> Not long after, the king was crushed beneath stampeding wildebeest. The prince escaped only by chance, scrambling along cliff and canyon.<br /> Then he fell into a wall of Thorns.<br /> <br /> Years later, a man returns to the savannah, stronger and wiser. His choice of clothing is odd: a flame-red mantle and a lion's skin, so vivid and soft you would think it was still on the beast. He has endured much, he proclaims to the tribe, but none of it broke his spirit.<br /> Not long after, the king is burned to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T06:55:24-08:00","id":403263,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;In the jungle you must wait, until the dice roll five or eight&quot;</i><br /> <br /> It had seemed innocent enough. Just a game, hidden away beneath the roots of the tree your father pulled up to make an extension to his shoe factory. You couldn't explain why it was locked and chained in a chest, or why your heart hammered out a tattoo against your rib cage. Made of carved wood, with a green orb of glass marking the goal- filled with an unusual, swirling smoke just a shade or two darker than the glass itself. The pieces are easy enough to identify, carved seemingly from old ivory as they are- an elephant, a rhinoceros, a crocodile, and a monkey. Roll the dice, play the game, and pray to whatever you hold dear that you live. Land on the wrong spot, and the game isn't content to stay on the board, roll the wrong number, and expect to be hunted. Cheat- and pray that if you do you are <b><i>never</i></b> caught -and you'll find yourself in dire straits.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You think that mosquitoes, monkeys, and lions are bad? That is just the beginning. I've seen things you've only seen in your nightmares. Things you can't even imagine. Things you can't even see. There are things that hunt you in the night. Then something screams. Then you hear them eating, and you hope to God you aren't dessert. Afraid? You don't know what afraid is.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T22:59:37-08:00","id":408629,"title":"","content":"This story begins with a kind girl. A girl who wanders into the forest, meaning no harm.<br /> What she doesn't know is that this land belongs to Him, is roamed by the not-humans that he calls 'family.'<br /> They look like people, but they aren't <i>really</i>, are they? They belong in the world of fang and claw, wing and hoof. And it's not hard at all to reveal their true forms, if one only knows how. (The girl learns this, much to her sorrow.)<br /> But the Beasts are not cruel. They let her stay with them, working for food and board, if she agrees to protect their secret. And if she is careful to stay away from Him- their patriarch, their master, their god.<br /> For it is his fault, you see. He cursed all of them, long ago.<br /> And they will never be free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T09:45:14-08:00","id":409057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=408629#post408629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This story begins with a kind girl. A girl who wanders into the forest, meaning no harm.<br /> What she doesn't know is that this land belongs to Him, is roamed by the not-humans that he calls 'family.'<br /> They look like people, but they aren't <i>really</i>, are they? They belong in the world of fang and claw, wing and hoof. And it's not hard at all to reveal their true forms, if one only knows how. (The girl learns this, much to her sorrow.)<br /> But the Beasts are not cruel. They let her stay with them, working for food and board, if she agrees to protect their secret. And if she is careful to stay away from Him- their patriarch, their master, their god.<br /> For it is his fault, you see. He cursed all of them, long ago.<br /> And they will never be free.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fruits Basket!<br /> <br /> For some, being taken is a blessing. That is how it started for this young boy, a slave. They saw potential in him, one they could mold to their higher purposes. They trained him, taught him their ways. He did well, and was told great things. He was the chosen one, the one who would bring balance. Soon, he started wanting more, and the dream turned to a nightmare. His masters held him back, lied to him, betrayed him. When the time came for his escape, he did it by force, ridding the world of his former masters, or so he thought. His escape did not come without cost. His body was blackened, and forced into an artificial shell. Now he is the master, and hunts down the remnants of his former master's influence, and discovering they they may not be as banished as he had thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T19:08:02-08:00","id":409493,"title":"","content":"Star Wars?<br /> <br /> Here's one I was just introduced to by Chris Stuckmann. Could be a story of the beginnings of a Vigil, too;<br /> <br /> Gather 'round, children, and let me speak of the story of the Grieving Guest, a most caring friend. A special friend, with crows feet for hands and a funny hat, with the grin of a bear. It's his only expression-the Guest's body isn't his real one, it's his way of talking to you, in that lovely little sound by which he gets his proper name He loves you, you see-he so wants to know people, the bits that remind him of his empty home, his broken home. He loves you, because you can break just like his his home does, under stress, how you react to sadness and despair, and how he can live in you, too. That's what he really wants, to be let into that dark place left behind when someone loved is gone, and to curl up there, and never leave-not that he does otherwise. He only leaves when his new house is utterly broken,and then he takes the house with him to add to his own bleak estate.<br /> <br /> He <i>can't</i> leave, now-what was once his house is now his warden. Her little child was too clever for the Guest, too prepared, and his house wasn't taken by the grief like he is. He's stuck-feasting on worms, moldering in her basement, truly homeless. But he lives, and he still craves a home-for if it's a word, or if it's a book...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T01:16:48-08:00","id":409787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=409057#post409057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fruits Basket!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> -<br /> The man wakes up on a mortuary slab, his flesh greyed and tattered by...something. He doesn't know what.<br /> All he knows is that he's forgotten who he once was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T06:05:01-08:00","id":411349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=409787#post409787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> -<br /> The man wakes up on a mortuary slab, his flesh greyed and tattered by...something. He doesn't know what.<br /> All he knows is that he's forgotten who he once was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Planescape: Torment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:32:26-08:00","id":413571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=411349#post411349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Planescape: Torment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> -<br /> She is a Dancer, thin as a feather. She is an illusion, whiter than white, gliding over the stage like a bird. She has belonged to the Fae for a very long time.<br /> Then her rival arrives, trying to steal her place. Trying to <i>overshadow </i>her, or so the voices insist.<br /> But the Dancer does not give up. She can do better, she knows it. She can be perfect.<br /> The hunger, the blood, the shame- what does any of it really matter? She will suffer for her art, like all great performers. She will excel further.<br /> <br /> This is the story of a Changeling who never left her prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T21:08:30-08:00","id":413686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=409493#post409493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Star Wars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=413571#post413571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She is a Dancer, thin as a feather. She is an illusion, whiter than white, gliding over the stage like a bird. She has belonged to the Fae for a very long time.<br /> Then her rival arrives, trying to steal her place. Trying to <i>overshadow </i>her, or so the voices insist.<br /> But the Dancer does not give up. She can do better, she knows it. She can be perfect.<br /> The hunger, the blood, the shame- what does any of it really matter? She will suffer for her art, like all great performers. She will excel further.<br /> <br /> This is the story of a Changeling who never left her prison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Swan?<br /> <br /> Emmet was just like everyone else. He liked the shows everyone liked, he listened to the popular music everyone listened too, he cheered for the local sorts team like everyone else. Then one day after work at the construction site, he fell into a hole in the building they were demolishing, and suddenly everything changed. Whisked across worlds by bizarre beings who saw things differently than he. Where he had conformity, they had creativity, where he saw objects, they saw parts. When he finally returned to his own world, he was hunted by the same people he used to be like. No longer normal, and not entirely like the others, it was by walking the line between he truly found that he was the greatest, most interesting, and most important person of all times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T20:52:05-08:00","id":414813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=413686#post413686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Whisked across worlds by bizarre beings who saw things differently than he. Where he had conformity, they had creativity, where he saw objects, they saw parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, that is a great metaphor. And you're right about it being Black Swan.<br /> -<br /> An amateur detective is called to England by a worried husband. His wife has secluded herself behind thick curtains, and refuses to tell anyone why. She begins to eat only raw meat, and speaks cryptically of a curse, a curse from which she cannot be saved.<br /> And as the detective wanders down dark passageways, discovering the secrets their ancient manor hides, she begins to understand that they are not alone...<br /> <br /> &quot;There are some doors that must never be opened. There are some secrets that must never be known.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:35:32-07:00","id":433049,"title":"","content":"Deep within the Hedge and into the walls of Arcadia lies a place that even other True Fae speak of with hints of fear. A mansion that is clean and calm on the surface, but hides secrets that could only have been conceived in the worst of nightmares. The Gentry which resides and rules there has an air of a well read gentleman, but should you peer behind the Mask, you will see brief glimpses of shining blades and hear the wet squirming of bloated leeches. This gentleman insists his methods of experimentation are based on science and reason. He is eerily polite, even as he transforms you inch by inch into a monster. He has a whole legion of abominations under his command, but every so often, he chooses someone who he can\u2019t break to wear his Prop. Said \u201cspecial\u201d subjects are pitted against the legions of monsters under the promise of being granted freedom should they provide satisfactory data. That day almost never comes, however. And night after night, broken bones after spilled guts, these victims make their way through the mansion and back to the real world. The Prop never comes back with them, but some grow a mad fondness for the power the artifact gave them and learn to create copies. And thus, the Splatterhouse grows.<br /> <br /> (In game terms, the Terror Mask is a Fae Title in Prop form. It belongs to a True Fae with Wyrd 9. Treat someone who is wearing the Mask as a True Fae Actor, with all the powers and weaknesses that come with that, such as spending glamour to heal wounds, dream warping and invoking new Contract clauses on the fly. You can create Hedgespun items, unlike other True Fae. The Computer, Expression and Empathy Skills do not suffer limitations, and your creativity is unaffected. Apply the following characteristics, which overwrite supernatural templates as long as the Mask is being worn. The Mien Blessings may vary. You gain Bloodthirsty as an additional Vice.)<br /> <br /> Seeming: Ogre<br /> <br /> Attributes: Power 8, Finesse 6, Resistance 7<br /> <br /> Bonus Merits: Ambidextrous, Gunslinger, Quick Draw, Disarm, Demolisher 3, Frenzied Assault 5, Hedge Duelsit 5, Heavy Weapons (All Weapons) 5, Two Weapons 4, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Striking Looks +2, Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Harvest (Emotions 5, Goblin Fruit 5), Lethal Mien, Charmed Life, Armored Mien 1/1<br /> <br /> Wyrd: 9<br /> Contracts: Darkness 6, Stone 6, Separation 3, Moon 5, Artifice 5, Animation 3, Fleeting Autumn 1, Goblin (Shooter's Bargain, Delayed Harm)<br /> Max Glamour/Per Turn: 50/10<br /> Frailties: determined by the Storyteller<br /> <br /> Mien Blessings: Improvised Mayhem (Bloodbrute), Obdurate Skin (Stonebones), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/163507-walking-shadows-seemings-and-kiths\">Weapons</a> (Soldier)<br /> <br /> Fae Aspects: Immortal Flesh and Ruled By Passion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-08-2015, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:16:19-07:00","id":436033,"title":"","content":"They say you can never really go home again. That was certainly his case. They came in the night, calling him friend, and in the morning, he went willingly under a contract. But friends they were not. They were haughty, cruel, and obstinate. They would march him to his limit, then continue for hours beyond. Yet horrible as they were, he grew to find loyalty to them. He had opportunities to go back, but could never do it. &quot;I can't leave,&quot; he thought, &quot;I've signed a contract.&quot; <br /> <br /> Eventually, his term of service was over, and their task complete, though not without cost. Some among their number perished, as did his innocence. His body returned, but his mind was ever elsewhere. He kept the tokens of his journey ever close at hand, and longed to hear them summon him once more. To hear them say, &quot;We need our burglar.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T07:47:01-07:00","id":450431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=436033#post436033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They say you can never really go home again. That was certainly his case. They came in the night, calling him friend, and in the morning, he went willingly under a contract. But friends they were not. They were haughty, cruel, and obstinate. They would march him to his limit, then continue for hours beyond. Yet horrible as they were, he grew to find loyalty to them. He had opportunities to go back, but could never do it. &quot;I can't leave,&quot; he thought, &quot;I've signed a contract.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eventually, his term of service was over, and their task complete, though not without cost. Some among their number perished, as did his innocence. His body returned, but his mind was ever elsewhere. He kept the tokens of his journey ever close at hand, and longed to hear them summon him once more. To hear them say, &quot;We need our burglar.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Hobbit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T09:30:03-07:00","id":450524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=450431#post450431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Hobbit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! I thought it would be fun to cast Bilbo as something close to a loyalist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T18:53:01-07:00","id":452208,"title":"","content":"A slew of high-profile sports stars find themselves weakened, their strength, speed, and coordination sapped from their bodies. Upon discovering that the Gentry have stolen their abilities to play, a retired star makes them bet: should he win them in a game, they return what was stolen. But if he loses, they take him to Arcadia as their eternal slave. Now it's up to him and a team of beast changelings to defeat the otherworldly menace in the most high-stakes game of their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:26:53-07:00","id":454157,"title":"","content":"Had to read it twice to recognize it was Space Jam.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> Screaming... that's the only warning most people get before it happens. Massive explosions, unexplained natural disasters, or electronic devices over loading. Sometimes the screaming lasts for only a few seconds... other times it can go on for 10 whole minutes! You've heard the stories, people emitting death rays from their hands and blowing their foes to pieces in the blink of an eye. Warriors who gleam like the sun, or change their forms dramatically before your eyes. Many people die in the presence of these warriors, but sometimes they don't stay dead.<br /> <br /> The foes these warriors face have to be seen to be believed. From colossal weremonkeys, to albino lizards, giant midgets, clockwork teenagers, parasitic insects, elastic starfish, and even hairless cats!<br /> <br /> The land resembles our own Earth to a certain degree, but those who know of its existence refer to it simply as The Dragon World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-23-2015, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T00:20:05-07:00","id":458726,"title":"","content":"He lurks in the dark corners of a glittering city, where legions of smiling, hollow people act out his gaudy technicolor fantasies. If you're lucky, you'll never see his face, but he knows yours well, and he wants to make you a star. He knows that you have what it takes, if only you didn't have so many things holding you back. He'll take your worries, fears, and regrets, and lock them away in a shiny blue box. From time to time he may take a little more than that, but surely your memories are a small price to pay for a life of glamour.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are those ungrateful souls who refuse to play the roles in which they have been cast. The man in the shadows is nothing if not patient; he sends his loyal marionettes to show these uncooperative few the error of their ways - gently at first, and then with a firmer hand. In the end, however, he knows that even he makes mistakes sometimes; to those who resolutely refuse to follow his direction he at last bestows a key to match their box of troubles, and watches with righteous glee as they destroy themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 03-27-2015, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T02:26:50-07:00","id":458766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=458726#post458726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He lurks in the dark corners of a glittering city, where legions of smiling, hollow people act out his gaudy technicolor fantasies. If you're lucky, you'll never see his face, but he knows yours well, and he wants to make you a star. He knows that you have what it takes, if only you didn't have so many things holding you back. He'll take your worries, fears, and regrets, and lock them away in a shiny blue box. From time to time he may take a little more than that, but surely your memories are a small price to pay for a life of glamour.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are those ungrateful souls who refuse to play the roles in which they have been cast. The man in the shadows is nothing if not patient; he sends his loyal marionettes to show these uncooperative few the error of their ways - gently at first, and then with a firmer hand. In the end, however, he knows that even he makes mistakes sometimes; to those who resolutely refuse to follow his direction he at last bestows a key to match their box of troubles, and watches with righteous glee as they destroy themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mullholland Drive?<br /> <br /> 'He wants slaves, but then don't they all? He is not a crafter of worlds but of infinities, of a universe of darkness and struggle. Worlds are merely baubles kicked along in his great game. He conjures rivals and pretenders to his gilded throne, he plots a million upon a million intrigues.<br /> <br /> Some playthings he twists into alien simulacrum; elfin armies on the brink of oblivion, greenskined beasts and ogres to prey upon the weak. Sometimes, he crafts daemons to assail the masses and doubts to stymie the strong. He is the source of mankind's woe and the font of their hope. They pray to him, venerate him. Volunteer themselves for the armies in his pantomime wars.<br /> <br /> They call him Father. They call him God. They call him Emperor.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":4871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","user":"Malkydel","date":". 03-27-2015, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T10:33:31-07:00","id":459148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=458766#post458766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mullholland Drive?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=458766#post458766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'He wants slaves, but then don't they all? He is not a crafter of worlds but of infinities, of a universe of darkness and struggle. Worlds are merely baubles kicked along in his great game. He conjures rivals and pretenders to his gilded throne, he plots a million upon a million intrigues.<br /> <br /> Some playthings he twists into alien simulacrum; elfin armies on the brink of oblivion, greenskined beasts and ogres to prey upon the weak. Sometimes, he crafts daemons to assail the masses and doubts to stymie the strong. He is the source of mankind's woe and the font of their hope. They pray to him, venerate him. Volunteer themselves for the armies in his pantomime wars.<br /> <br /> They call him Father. They call him God. They call him Emperor.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Warhammer (40k)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T10:57:53-07:00","id":459189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=459148#post459148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Warhammer (40k)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:04:12-07:00","id":462665,"title":"","content":"She used to be a chorus girl, languishing in obscurity, and longing for the spotlight. At night, she took singing lessons. In sleep he came to her, and in those dreams he sang. The voice called to her, spoke her name. Soon she found that she only wished to dream again, to her his song, and to learn to sing as he did. Eventually she wanted only to be his student. He appeared to her in a mirror, and took her to a land of darkness and song. Away from the garish light of day she learned his music, the music of the night. But she was too curious, and saw his true face, a face that would forever haunt her mind. When the time came for her to return to her own world, she found her song powerful, and her memories of the other place were more terrible than wonderful. When her angel of music came again to teach her, she now resisted. Having seen his face, she could only draw back in fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T15:21:17-07:00","id":462742,"title":"","content":"You know, using lyrics makes it quite apparent. Phantom of the Opera. Great- now I'm imagining Erik as a Charlatan who's absolutely perplexed and tormented by having developed genuine emotion; as the fluff hints they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T15:06:35-07:00","id":469634,"title":"","content":"Not all True Fae assume forms inspired by classical fairy tale symbols such as knights, witches and dragons. Some like to go for something more modern, and even imitate pop culture. One of these True Fae fancies himself a superhero straight from comic books. He used to have a whole City filled with changeling sidekicks, hobgoblin mutants and True Fae super villains. He used to think the entire universe revolved around him and his impeccable righteousness, even as threw temper tantrums, demanded to be the center of attention and refused to be questioned. However, he started visiting Earth more frequently, saw how complex things really were and how even humans could be heroes sometimes. He began to think of others as more than just playthings, eventually abandoned his City and freed his prisoners. With two Titles left and a Beast Windwing as his trusted sidekick, he set out to protect the innocent and defenseless, wherever they may be. He calls himself The Tick.<br /> <br /> Virtue: Justice<br /> Vice: Childish<br /> Seeming: Ogre<br /> Mien Blessings: Obdurate Skin (Stonebones), Sundering Talons (Render), Improvised Mayhem (Bloodbrute)<br /> <br /> Attributes: Power 7, Finesse 4, Resistance 7<br /> <br /> Mental Skills: Academics 2, Crafts 2, Computer 1, Medicine 1, Occult 2, Politics 0, Investigation 3, Science 1<br /> Physical Skills: Athletics (Running, Jumping) 6, Brawl 6, Drive 0, Firearms 0, Larceny 2, Stealth 2, Survival 4, Weaponry (Improvised) 6<br /> Social Skills: Animal Ken 1, Empathy 3, Expression (Speeches) 2, Intimidation (Crazy) 3, Persuasion (Friendliness) 3, Socialize 2, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> Merits: Ambidextrous, Quick Draw, Disarm, Demolisher 3, Aggressive Striking 4, Hedge Duelist 5, Heavy Weapons (All Weapons) 5, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Striking Looks +2, Fast Reflexes 3, Fleet of Foot 3, Iron Stamina 3, Harvest (Pledges 5, Goblin Fruit 5), Hollow 7 (Size 2, Amenities 3, Garden 2), Lethal Mien, Charmed Life, Armored Mien 1/1, Acute Mien Sense (Hearing) 2, Golem\u2019s Palate, True Friend (Arthur)<br /> <br /> Wyrd: 7<br /> Contracts: Stone 5, Separation 5, Forge 5, Oath And Punishment 5, Vainglory 3, Dream 2, Goblin (Delayed Harm, Diviner\u2019s Madness, Fool\u2019s Gold)<br /> Max Glamour/Per Turn: 20/7<br /> Frailties: any attack made against his antennae (major bane), cannot refuse an offer of food (minor taboo), cannot harm those he perceives as innocent (minor taboo)<br /> <br /> Fae Aspects:<br /> <br /> Immortal Flesh<br /> <br /> Change of Heart: The True Fae are entities almost embodied by their passions and vices, with higher morality and self-denial little more than a whim to them. For them, passion is virtue, and the denial of passion an affectation. Their supernaturally amoral nature is reflected in an inverted ability to regain Willpower. They regain one Willpower point from indulging their Virtue, but refresh their whole pool when satiating their Vice.<br /> <br /> The Tick, on the other hand, has spent enough time on the mortal world to absorb part of humanity\u2019s nature. He can remain on Earth without suffering damage, regains Willpower normally, can harvest Glamour from selfless emotions, can create Hedgespun items and does not have the Skill limits of most True Fae. However, his mindset is still very much alien, and thus he has no Morality or Clarity meter, nor can his strange thought processes be represented by Derangements, as is the case with the other True Fae.<br /> <br /> Titles: Guardian Of Justice (Actor), The Arthropod Aegis (Prop)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-05-2015, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T18:11:44-07:00","id":469706,"title":"","content":"There is a legend among the Lost, of a great, swordsman who was born from death itself. From the age of 6 he was trained in the ways of swordsmanship and war, killing his first man before he was even 10 years old. The swordsman found comrades in arms, putting an end to a century of war and rising to the top of command among his new allies. Then it all went horribly wrong. The swordsman had a friend who longed to be king... so great was his desire that he would sacrifice his entire army to achieve his ambition. The swordsman and all his friends were dragged forcefully to Arcadia, where he saw them eaten alive by by the denizens of the that hellish place. The traitor joined the ranks of the True Fae, and though he suffered terrible injuries, the swordsman escaped.<br /> <br /> Now he is out for blood, and will not rest until the man who betrayed them dies painfully. He carries a great iron sword, large enough to cleave a man and his horse in two with a single blow. Is is a member of the Summer Court, or a Changeling turned Hunter? Nobody is certain anymore; he does not go into battle with strategy in mind... he just goes <i>berserk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1Df8P2KZi4\" data-code=\"W1Df8P2KZi4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/W1Df8P2KZi4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2015, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T04:46:52-07:00","id":470055,"title":"","content":"Most people either focus on being good or evil. But what happens if you're in between, or if one side just slightly outweighs the other? What do you think happens to those people when the meet their fate? Do they go the purgatory, to wander amidst limbo until they repent? Perhaps, but sometimes there is another option, a place for those who are only slightly more evil than righteous. Slightly more naughty, slightly more rebellious... slightly damned.<br /> <br /> Technically it's not a level of hell. In fact, it's located outside the gates of hell, but within close enough proximity to be visited by those who reside there. Technically, yes, it does have demons that wander its land, but they're much less violent than the denizens of hell. In fact the only real tortures they perform includes bullying or pranks, so if your made of sterner stuff or have a broad sense of humor, they might actually be tolerable. But it's still a dull and dreary place, and the demons can get on people's nerves after a time. There is a way out, back to the world of the living... but it's located within the depths of hell itself. The choice is yours; do you assault the legions of hell in search of the portal back home, or do you stay here in this &quot;ring of the slightly damned?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-07-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T02:25:41-07:00","id":471028,"title":"","content":"I think Griffith would be a Bright One.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=470055#post470055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> slightly damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, nice title drop.<br /> -<br /> When she was young, a girl was taken by the Fae. All the way across the Hedge, they sensed the fear that she caused in those around her, the minds warped by her nightmarish presence- and they <i>hungered</i>. They locked her in a cage of eternal winter, and fed on the girl's heart.<br /> She was more fortunate than most captives, for a knight came to save her. And in the warmth of the human world, what did it matter that she could vanish? That she <b>knew</b> the emotions of others, laid bare like organs on a tray?<br /> But the Fae are not cheated.<br /> Years later, her knight emerges from a ice-bound lake. His eyes, once so fiery, have darkened with cold. Anger shreds the Snowskin's heart like a blizzard, animating his drowned and broken body. Through a voice harsh with disuse, he asks the Mirrorskin for help.<br /> She accepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T13:39:09-07:00","id":488650,"title":"","content":"Inspired by the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=163280#post163280\">Fae version of Homestuck</a>, I decided to come up with further details of the Fae-ifyng, Seemings/kiths for the Beta Kids and Trolls, plus stats for Lord English.<br /> <br /> Assume that the objects which contain the code for running Sburb are legendary Tokens. They allow changelings and mortals alike to bring pieces of the Hedge and Arcadia into Earth. Once your house is taken into the Hedge, it becomes a Hollow. From there, you explore the Hedge and earn Grist by defeating enemy hobgoblins and helping friendly hobgoblins. Grist serves as Glamour and GMC Experience Points, which you may use to create epic Hedgespun Tokens, sign Contracts and improve your Traits. When you defeat the Denizen (a powerful hobgoblin), you gain enough Grist to enter an Arcadian Realm in the form of a chess planet. There, you will temporarily have the powers of a True Fae, while an army of chess piece-like beings straight from your dreams take sides on a massive battle. The Light always loses, and its up to the players to defeat the Dark. If you win, you may return to Earth as a changeling, never being able to perfectly adjust to the mundane after what you went through. If the players lose, it's Game Over. The Arcadian Realm resets, the old players are sent to another Arcadian Realm and new players are selected. But if there is no True Fae, who is the Keeper of the players?<br /> <br /> The Wyrd itself.<br /> <br /> Think about it. All that the Wyrd/Sburb care about is the Tale. The changelings play their part, whether they want to or not.<br /> <br /> Here are what the Wyrd/Sburb could have changed the characters into:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 50px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Character</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Seeming</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kiths</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">John</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Fairest</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths#Lionhearted\" target=\"_blank\">Lionhearted</a>/Airtouched</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Dave</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Wizened</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Soldier/Telluric</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Rose</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Darkling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Moonborn/Witchtooth</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Jade</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Elemental</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Woodblood/Soldier/Inventor</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Karkat</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Wizened</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Soldier/Hardshell</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Equius</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Ogre</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Render/Artist</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Gamzee</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Darkling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Moonborn/<a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths#Berserker\" target=\"_blank\">Berserker</a>/Muse</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Nepeta</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Beast</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Hunterheart/Artist</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Kanaya</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Fairest</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Bright One/Artist</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Terezi</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Darkling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Antiquarian/<a href=\"http://1d4chan.org/wiki/Changeling_Homebrew_Kiths#Barrister\" target=\"_blank\">Barrister</a></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Sollux</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Wizened</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=421046#post421046\">Coder</a>/Venombite</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Eridan</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Beast</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Swimmerskin/Soldier</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Feferi</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Elemental</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Waterborn/Truefriend</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Aradia</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Darkling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Antiquarian/Gravewight</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Vriska</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Darkling</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Whisperwisp/Venombite/Gameplayer</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Tavros</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Elemental</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 3px; padding: 1px\">Metalflesh/Gameplayer/Chimera</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> Name: Lord English<br /> <br /> Virtue: Implacable<br /> <br /> Vice: Destroyer<br /> <br /> Seeming: Elemental<br /> <br /> Attributes: Power 10, Finesse 4, Resistance 10<br /> <br /> Mental Skills: Academics (History) 3, Computer 1, Crafts 1, Investigation 3, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Politics 0, Science (Time Travel) 3<br /> <br /> Physical Skills: Athletics 3, Brawl 6, Drive 0, Firearms (Assault Rifle) 8, Larceny 1, Stealth 0, Survival 1, Weaponry (Cane) 6<br /> <br /> Social Skills: Animal Ken 0, Empathy 1, Expression 0, Intimidation (Huge) 8, Persuasion 3, Socialize 0, Streetwise 4, Subterfuge 4<br /> <br /> Merits: Encyclopedic Knowledge (Science, Intimidation), Eidetic Memory, Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Ambidextrous, Fast Reflexes 3, Iron Stamina 3, Harvest (Emotions 5, Dreams 5), Armored Mien 1/1, Dream Combat 5, Combat Marksmanship 5, Rigid Mask 2, Lethal Mien, Demolisher 3, Charmed Life, Striking Looks +2<br /> <br /> Health: 20 (Size 10)<br /> <br /> Willpower: 10<br /> <br /> Defense: 4<br /> <br /> Initiative Mod: 17<br /> <br /> Speed: 19<br /> <br /> Wyrd: 10<br /> <br /> Contracts: Forge 5, Hours 5, Darkness 5, Stone 5, Vainglory 5, Control The Elements (Time) 5, Communion With The Elements (Time) 5, Dream 5, Goblin (Fair Entrance, Delayed Harm, Call The Wild Hunt)<br /> <br /> Maximum Glamour/per Turn: 100/15<br /> <br /> Mien Blessings: Obdurate Skin (Stonebones), Spurious Stature (Gargantuan), The Voice Of Ice (Snowskin), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/163507-walking-shadows-seemings-and-kiths\">Terrestrial Might</a> (Earthbones)<br /> <br /> Fae Aspects:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/343836-fae-actors-2e-hack\">Immortal Flesh And Ruled By Passion</a><br /> <br /> Already Here: Lord English and his Props can exist simultaneously in multiple locations across different realities, including Earth, the Hedge and Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Titles: The Emerald Terror (Actor), The Great Tick Tock (Realm), The Felt (Wisp), The Green Sun (Prop), Cairo Overcoat (Prop)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/343836-fae-actors-2e-hack?p=487639#post487639\">Fae Influences:</a><br /> <br /> Sands Of Time, Hands Of Fate, The Heart\u2019s Many Strings (Terror &amp; Respect)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-30-2015, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T09:19:10-07:00","id":491695,"title":"","content":"I really think that Feferi would be a Waterborn. There's this sense of <i>oddity</i> that distinguishes her from the other trolls, as if she lives in a different world. Her backstory is heavily tied to the sea as a predatory, dark thing- a place beyond human comprehension. She's a bright pretty fish, but she is also the heir to hulking Cthulhu-esque devourers and raging high-blood.<br /> <br /> Maybe Vriska is dual-kithed? She does, after all, have all of the levels. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:36:19-07:00","id":491744,"title":"","content":"When our hero first met the girl, she was skating through his dreams, taking a shortcut, she said. He loved her, couldn't turn away from her, the girl with the hair of many colors. Later he found out it was her mien coming through, her polychromatic nature so strong a mere mask couldn't hide it. She said she was running, that others would come for her, seven in all. Our hero swore to protect her. First was the elemental onieropomp, pulling succubi from dreams as distractions and throwing flames in a fight, but hardly a match for our hero. Second was the ogre skateboarder, far greater in might, and with a motley of similar-looking brutes at his beck and call, but too tied to the rules of bets and dares, which proved his undoing. Third was the fairest bassist, muse at his side, who was only beaten when his old masters dragged him back for some arcane infraction to do with eating. Fourth was the jealous beast, bitter in broken loyalty, wielding the chains that used to bind her as weapons, who could only be overcome by her old love. Fifth and sixth were the wizened DJ and his fetch, acting as one, too powerful to be overcome in combat, but willing to decide the outcome in a battle of the bands. And seventh? Seventh was the Other that took her, or at least, one of It's Actors, who waltzed in with a grin and took her, no trouble. Our hero tried to fight, and was slain. But in the realm of the dead, he got a second chance, and took it, and beat the Other, and saved her. Time would only tell if the victory was worth the cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:50:07-07:00","id":491757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>'He wants slaves, but then don't they all? He is not a crafter of worlds but of infinities, of a universe of darkness and struggle. Worlds are merely baubles kicked along in his great game. He conjures rivals and pretenders to his gilded throne, he plots a million upon a million intrigues.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Some playthings he twists into alien simulacrum; elfin armies on the brink of oblivion, greenskined beasts and ogres to prey upon the weak. Sometimes, he crafts daemons to assail the masses and doubts to stymie the strong. He is the source of mankind's woe and the font of their hope. They pray to him, venerate him. Volunteer themselves for the armies in his pantomime wars.</i><br /> <br /> <i>They call him Father. They call him God. They call him Emperor.'</i> </div> </div> </div>Did...did you make the Emperor an Avatar of Tzeentch?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://gendertrender.files.wordpress.com/2014/12/heresytrain.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T13:28:28-07:00","id":491906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=491744#post491744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When our hero first met the girl, she was skating through his dreams, taking a shortcut, she said. He loved her, couldn't turn away from her, the girl with the hair of many colors. Later he found out it was her mien coming through, her polychromatic nature so strong a mere mask couldn't hide it. She said she was running, that others would come for her, seven in all. Our hero swore to protect her. First was the elemental onieropomp, pulling succubi from dreams as distractions and throwing flames in a fight, but hardly a match for our hero. Second was the ogre skateboarder, far greater in might, and with a motley of similar-looking brutes at his beck and call, but too tied to the rules of bets and dares, which proved his undoing. Third was the fairest bassist, muse at his side, who was only beaten when his old masters dragged him back for some arcane infraction to do with eating. Fourth was the jealous beast, bitter in broken loyalty, wielding the chains that used to bind her as weapons, who could only be overcome by her old love. Fifth and sixth were the wizened DJ and his fetch, acting as one, too powerful to be overcome in combat, but willing to decide the outcome in a battle of the bands. And seventh? Seventh was the Other that took her, or at least, one of It's Actors, who waltzed in with a grin and took her, no trouble. Our hero tried to fight, and was slain. But in the realm of the dead, he got a second chance, and took it, and beat the Other, and saved her. Time would only tell if the victory was worth the cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Scott Pilgrim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:19:07-07:00","id":492011,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Why, why would God allow this to exist? What horrible sin could condone such a fate? Whisked away from their homes and brought to a brightly lit, sterile room. They find they have no limbs, being forced to sit in their new location and do little more than glance around their environment. The first thing that confronts them is that insufferable, citrus sphere who's infinite capacity lungs allow it ramble off incoherently for incalculable amounts of time. It states the obvious, it makes the crudest of jokes, stupidest of faces and most irritating of sounds. Only once the prisoners are driven to the breaking point does the sweet release finally come. The only word of warning they get is.. 'knife!'</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:35:50-07:00","id":492041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=492011#post492011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Why, why would God allow this to exist? What horrible sin could condone such a fate? Whisked away from their homes and brought to a brightly lit, sterile room. They find they have no limbs, being forced to sit in their new location and do little more than glance around their environment. The first thing that confronts them is that insufferable, citrus sphere who's infinite capacity lungs allow it ramble off incoherently for incalculable amounts of time. It states the obvious, it makes the crudest of jokes, stupidest of faces and most irritating of sounds. Only once the prisoners are driven to the breaking point does the sweet release finally come. The only word of warning they get is.. 'knife!'</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Annoying Orange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T09:00:13-07:00","id":492617,"title":"","content":"Your Keeper was a Storykeeper, finding and claiming all the stories ever told, and bringing hapless humans in to act them out, over and over and over again, for its amusement. You always wanted to act, but not like this.<br /> <br /> As the story starts, you're a young boy, leaving his mother behind to start a grand adventure. Then you're an angry young man. Then a slightly older, but still angry man, and this leads to your doom. You are defeated, but do not die, and spend the rest of the story unrecognizable, the nemesis of a new batch of characters who actually get to win. In the end, you give your life to reclaim yourself, and then it starts all over again, and you're back to being the sad boy.<br /> <br /> Finally, you've escaped. You can't go back. You don't WANT to go back. You can't bear the thought of lying there, one more time, limbs sliced off, burning next to a river of lava and hearing that awfully-scripted line:<br /> <br /> &quot;YOU WERE MY BROTHER, ANAKIN!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:37:28-07:00","id":495652,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">So, I have been thinking about the relationship between Batman and the Joker, and how it could be translated into Changeling terms.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">1) Joker is the Keeper: </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">When young Bruce Wayne and his parents took a wrong turn after watching the Zorro movie, they were separated and Bruce ended up in the Hedge. He was taken by the Joker, at the time possessing a Mien of a darkly beautiful gangster. Bruce was locked up inside an Arcadian Gotham and Joker left behind a Fetch that would grow up into the playboy persona that Batman displays in the comics when not fighting crime.<br /> <br /> The Gentry Joker fancies himself a criminal mastermind, using Ephemera to mimic police and rival criminals when not Feuding. However, Joker saw a special courage in young Bruce, and turned the boy into a vigilante changeling. Bruce, after years of studying his Keeper, takes Agency by conquering fear and using it against the Joker. The only thing Joker feared was losing control over his favorite plaything, so Bruce tricks the Joker into a Pledgebound game of wits. The Joker loses the game, and the sanction hits him hard, taking away his god-like powers for a short time. Bruce overpowers the Joker, throwing him into a vat of mystical chemicals. Bruce takes the opportunity to flee, developing the Darkling Seeming in the process.<br /> <br /> Once the Joker emerges from the vat, sees his deformity and that Bruce was gone, he goes mad, even by Gentry standards. The Joker develops a sick obsession with Bruce, often hiring Huntsmen to try and recapture him. Bruce eventually merges with his Fetch and uses his new resources to become a vigilante at large, wielding bat-themed Hedgespun. Bruce chose the bat as his symbol because he was very afraid of bats as a child, showing that fear no longer held power over him. Bruce becomes Batman, and defends the innocent from other monsters that mimic the rest of his Rogues Gallery from the comics.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>2) Batman is the Keeper:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jack was an engineer at a chemical plant, but decided to abandon this job to become a stand-up comedian. His new career cannot make ends meet, and he tries to make money to support his pregnant wife by leading a group of criminals into the plant. However, the other criminals are torn to shreds by a humanoid, armored, bat-like monster. This monster fancies himself a guardian of justice, and takes Jack into his Realm, which is an Arcadian version of the Arkham Asylum. In that Realm, whoever is caught by the Batman is turned into a changeling with features that symbolize their crimes and flaws, but they are given little to no chance of becoming better people.<br /> <br /> Jack is turned into a deformed clown as a reference to his failed comedy career. He manages to escape by conquering his fear and teaming up with the other changeling inmates, developing the Darkling Seeming in the process. However, when the escaped inmates see that enough time has passed in the real world to make the ones they cared about either die or forget about them, they all go mad. Jack himself snaps the hardest, and uses the hate the escaped inmates share for Batman to become their leader, forming a gang of super criminals with the goal of gathering enough resources to invade the Asylum and kill the Batman.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T23:15:59-07:00","id":495984,"title":"","content":"I prefer the second one; nice subversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:12:03-07:00","id":496403,"title":"","content":"That is pretty awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T06:17:07-07:00","id":501628,"title":"","content":"Lilith Weatherwax, full stop. She only needs to be added the fae subtype to fit as a perfect Keeper: a so-called Fairy Godmother who forces all individuals in her kingdom to live according with fairy tales and get their &quot;happily ever after&quot;... or else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:15:51-07:00","id":512106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=501628#post501628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith Weatherwax, full stop. She only needs to be added the fae subtype to fit as a perfect Keeper: a so-called Fairy Godmother who forces all individuals in her kingdom to live according with fairy tales and get their &quot;happily ever after&quot;... or else.</div> </div> </div> </div>But...but..that would make Granny True Fae too! She is scary enough!<br /> <br /> Elf Queen? She fits very well, especially given her connection to dreams and inability to create. But she's probably weaker True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:39:48-07:00","id":512120,"title":"","content":"Maybe Lilith is the one who became True Fae. Granny is still powerful and badass enough to face her sister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T20:11:44-07:00","id":512498,"title":"","content":"A newborn's mother dies giving birth to him, so the baby's father places him in a wolf den. He suckles alongside puppies, learning with every breath the language of fang and growl. A normal man might have feared for his son's safety, but this one is not normal- he is a sage, a shapeshifter who married a doe. Through his magic, the child is preserved.<br /> Yet all the sage's power cannot slay the <i>creature</i>, the mighty and bloodthirsty Beast coming to kill him.<br /> He hopes that, someday, his son will be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T04:46:46-07:00","id":512809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=512120#post512120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Lilith is the one who became True Fae. Granny is still powerful and badass enough to face her sister.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot decide if Granny would leave Fetch alone, recognising it has life and mind of it's own, or kill with heated poker because a) she hates 'unreal' things,b) nobody takes hers.<br /> <br /> If they were True Fae, they could be Nemesis of each other. As changelings, one could be Fetch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T18:34:01-07:00","id":516632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=512120#post512120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Lilith is the one who became True Fae. Granny is still powerful and badass enough to face her sister.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know who this &quot;Granny&quot; is... but let's see her take on Mother Goose!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T11:01:13-07:00","id":517186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=516632#post516632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know who this &quot;Granny&quot; is... but let's see her take on Mother Goose!</div> </div> </div> </div>(Facepalm) let's simply say it would be the most one sided fight since the rap battle between Beethoven and Justin Bieber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-20-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T07:34:36-07:00","id":521829,"title":"","content":"A bit of real life: sometimes in Australia, spiders rain down from the sky so thickly, that when they land, the ground is covered in webs. The webs stretch over the ground so completely, they look like snow-- and are sometimes referred to by locals as &quot;angel hair.&quot; If this is not Our Lady in Black, one of the Gentle folk sending her retinue to weave a carpet so she need not tread the common soil, I would be quite surprised: <a href=\"http://www.weather.com/series/great-outdoors/video/spiders-rain-down-on-austraila-cover-fields-in-sticky-webs?&amp;cm_ven=Email&amp;cm_cat=undefined\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.weather.com/series/great-..._cat=undefined</a><br /> <br /> Watch the video from the Weather Channel, if the spider-woven &quot;snow&quot; doesn't upset you, you're not paying attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:40:36-07:00","id":523164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=512498#post512498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A newborn's mother dies giving birth to him, so the baby's father places him in a wolf den. He suckles alongside puppies, learning with every breath the language of fang and growl. A normal man might have feared for his son's safety, but this one is not normal- he is a sage, a shapeshifter who married a doe. Through his magic, the child is preserved.<br /> Yet all the sage's power cannot slay the <i>creature</i>, the mighty and bloodthirsty Beast coming to kill him.<br /> He hopes that, someday, his son will be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The jungle book?<br /> <br /> He had always been a fighter. When he was young he taught the larger bullies not to pick on him. When he was older, he worked his natural talents in to a career. It wasn't until he finally made it to the big leagues that they found him. Their leader saw potential in him. This man was a fighter, but inside him was a monster waiting to be unleashed. They beat him down until he went willingly. Soon they realized what a mistake recruiting him was. There was indeed a monster in him. A raging, rampaging Dragon. They showed him how to unleash it and focus it's power. He made them the first targets, and made his way home. He was only gone for a few weeks, but was he forever changed? Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:56:24-07:00","id":523486,"title":"","content":"A storm rolled in on the island, and the entire mansion entered the world of the witch's game. She killed most of them before anyone noticed she was there, and the survivors found themselves whisked away for tea with her, where she admitted to her guests that she had just killed all of them just a moment ago.<br /> <br /> Ah, but there was only one among them who could refuse to accept that they had been murdered without even noticing it happen. This only amused the witch more, so she challenged the young man who had managed to doubt her story to a game. She would work to prove she and her magic were real, and he would struggle to prove it was not. He agreed to keep watching his family and even himself die over and over again, until he could prove the witch was never there.<br /> <br /> If only there were merely one mystery to solve...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T18:35:17-07:00","id":523830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=523164#post523164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The jungle book?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Paver's<i> Chronicles of Ancient Darkness.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=523486#post523486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A storm rolled in on the island, and the entire mansion entered the world of the witch's game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umineko, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T01:41:11-07:00","id":524182,"title":"","content":"Regarding Umineko, I admit it is a very interesting scenario. After all if Battler manages to rationalize the event through non.supernatural explanations, then the Wyrd will erase the Witch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-22-2015, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T05:21:28-07:00","id":524262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quynce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=521829#post521829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of real life: sometimes in Australia, spiders rain down from the sky so thickly, that when they land, the ground is covered in webs. The webs stretch over the ground so completely, they look like snow-- and are sometimes referred to by locals as &quot;angel hair.&quot; If this is not Our Lady in Black, one of the Gentle folk sending her retinue to weave a carpet so she need not tread the common soil, I would be quite surprised: <a href=\"http://www.weather.com/series/great-outdoors/video/spiders-rain-down-on-austraila-cover-fields-in-sticky-webs?&amp;cm_ven=Email&amp;cm_cat=undefined\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.weather.com/series/great-..._cat=undefined</a><br /> <br /> Watch the video from the Weather Channel, if the spider-woven &quot;snow&quot; doesn't upset you, you're not paying attention.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I will never step foot in Australia as long as I live! Raining a carpet of spiders gets you off my list of places I'd like to visit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-28-2016, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T10:15:46-07:00","id":524561,"title":"","content":"A young doctor finds his new workplace a bit...odd. Plumbing appears and disappears, his peers often lose themselves in fantastical daydreams, and sadistic pranks are not only allowed but encouraged. (But then, their victims are always a bit <i>tougher</i> than ordinary humans...) The only person who seems to understand what's going on is an cynical Chirugeon. He stays in the hospital because- despite its many sorrows and frustrations- being there allows him to help people who would otherwise fall through the cracks.<br /> With the Chirugeon's guidance (and a motley of rather neurotic Changelings), the doctor learns about himself, healing...and life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 05-22-2015, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T10:29:48-07:00","id":524566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=524561#post524561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A young doctor finds his new workplace a bit...odd. Plumbing appears and disappears, his peers often lose themselves in fantastical daydreams, and sadistic pranks are not only allowed but encouraged. (But then, their victims are always a bit <i>tougher</i> than ordinary humans...) The only person who seems to understand what's going on is an cynical Chirugeon. He stays in the hospital because- despite its many sorrows and frustrations- being there allows him to help people who would otherwise fall through the cracks.<br /> With the Chirugeon's guidance (and a motley of rather neurotic Changelings), the doctor learns about himself, healing...and life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scrubs? Heh, that made me chuckle if it is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T12:00:00-07:00","id":524609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=524566#post524566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scrubs? Heh, that made me chuckle if it is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Glad it made you happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:26:48-07:00","id":524741,"title":"","content":"Good one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T07:05:26-07:00","id":526607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=524182#post524182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Umineko, I admit it is a very interesting scenario. After all if Battler manages to rationalize the event through non.supernatural explanations, then the Wyrd will erase the Witch.</div> </div> </div> </div>And other witches are her feud rivals!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T17:15:00-07:00","id":653200,"title":"","content":"I was looking at my sheet for the Doctor as a True Fae, and it got me thinking. The Doctor is supposed to be a renegade among his species. So it follows that the Gentry version probably doesn't have Titles, so as to not attract the attention of other Gentry who want to enter a Feud or harm his loved ones. Because of this, he only has Wyrd 5, rather than Wyrd 5 + number of Titles. He willingly exiled himself from Arcadia and practically all Feuds, so he has different stats from a normal True Fae. He can't use Dream Warping, but he can use the other types of Oneiromancy like a changeling would. His Immortal Flesh has been transformed into the Regeneration from the show. Because of this, he is hurt by mundane weapons just like a human, and worse yet, he is still weak against cold iron and hand-forged iron. To compensate, his Empathy, Computer and Expression Skills don't have the limits of normal Gentry. He does not roll a chance die when attempting to create something new. He can harvest glamour from selfless emotions, but cannot receive glamour by breaking something or someone into the constituent parts. His Virtue and Vice work like those of a normal human, so he is not Ruled By Passion.<br /> <br /> Of note is that he knows how to create Hedgespun and Tokens. He likes to craft a new and thematic Hedgespun item to carry around when he Regenerates. He is so good at Hedgespinning that he does not need a Title in Realm form to mimic the TARDIS. His fae equivalent of the TARDIS is an epic level Hollow, with Size and Wards maxed out. The Hollow TARDIS is also Mobile, with the method of transportation being Space-Time Travel. The Hollow TARDIS can enter the Hedge, but it can't teleport once it is inside the Thorns, so the Doctor has to use other modes of transportation. It can still fly inside and outside the Hedge, but its altitude and speed aren't great, and its maneuverability is bad enough to be dangerous. Its heart/central processing unit is a mostly stationary, powerful and self-aware Hedgespun Automaton who tries communicating or seeing the outside world sometimes. K9 is another outstanding example of the Doctor's aptitude with Hedgespinning. The Sonic Screwdriver is a 5 dot Token focused on versatility instead of huge dice bonuses or grandiose powers. Its Drawback is that it doesn't work on one or a few materials common to whatever general area in space-time the Doctor is currently in, most famously wood. The Catch might be that, when a non fae uses it, they end up breaking or losing an important belonging, device or other item within the scene.<br /> <br /> The Daleks could be a small group of Border Reavers (Autumn Nightmares, page 122) which got so mutated that they had to build Hedgespun life-support systems. Because of their desire for revenge, they also equip themselves with extremely resistant armor and very cruel weapons. The other monsters, like the Weeping Angels, Silents and Cybermen, could be weirder-than-average hobgoblins. The Master is another Charlatan Gentry, but he is still a vicious, arrogant madman. The Companions are either Fae-Touched or straight-up changelings. There is no rule that says only Gentry with Realms can turn humans into changelings. Nergal (Autumn Nightmares, page 79) has no Realm, but still turned a mortal into Grandfather Thunder (1ed Core, page 338). The Doctor's Seeming is Fairest, but since he is not a changeling, it's only used for designing his Mien and for determining the benefits of 2ed Contracts. His kiths are <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/16XgmK7x1ZfRWF4cs-Ayw-Ih1YLgBmkFEs6klD81AfPY/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Maker, Smith and Telluric. </a></b><br /> <br /> EDIT: Then again, the Doctor supposedly stole his TARDIS, which is an obsolete Type 40. This makes me think the main engine/consciousness that powers his Hollow\u2019s space-time travel is a severed and abandoned Title in Prop form. To be frank, the TARDIS could be a lot of things.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: nothing wrong with making the TARDIS a Title in Realm form and the Doctor himself an Actor. That could attract the attention of other True Fae more often. However, the Sonic Screwdriver is not a Prop, since Props are supposed to perform their tasks perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-06-2015, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T19:04:54-07:00","id":696733,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any suggestions for adapting Luffy from One Piece as a changeling, according to 2ED rules? I'd say his Seeming is Fairest, and all his nakama swore the Motley Pledge. Pirate ships in general would be Mobile Hollows. What would his Durance and resulting Kith(s) be? Would the Gomu Gomu Fruit be an Arcadian goblin fruit that started his transformation into a changeling? Perhaps his Gomu Gomu powers don't come from his Kith, but a list of Contracts that mimic the effects of the Mirror, Stone and Control The Elements Contracts from 1ED. Furthermore, what equivalent to a Pirate King can a changeling become? Perhaps someone whose reputation of badassery is so far reaching among the fae that hobgoblins, Huntsmen, other changelings and the even the Gentry act with respect around him/her. Each changeling who seeks such recognition does it for different reasons, but Luffy wants it for the freedom it gives and the adventures it offers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T19:58:16-07:00","id":701599,"title":"","content":"Well the Devil Fruits are definitely some form of contract. Eat it and gain powers, but you will be forever changed in the process. In this particular case, maybe the Gum Gum Fruit contains the Contract of Elasticity. Luffy <i>might be</i> described as Gargantuan, being able to expand the size of his body, especially since he can literally inflate to giant proportions. For his Durance, let's look at his childhood with Ace and Sabo, where they took it upon themselves to beat the crap out of all the animals in the forest until they finally succeeded in defeating the apex predator who was a colossal tiger.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Pirate King, it would be in Luffy's own words.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't want to conquer anything, I think the person with the most freedom is the Pirate King.&quot;<br /> <br /> What could that mean? Well, what if he's a Changeling who is able to move and operate freely throughout Arcadia without being captured by the Gentry or becoming one of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-14-2015, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T21:33:51-07:00","id":701657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=701599#post701599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Devil Fruits are definitely some form of contract. Eat it and gain powers, but you will be forever changed in the process. In this particular case, maybe the Gum Gum Fruit contains the Contract of Elasticity. Luffy <i>might be</i> described as Gargantuan, being able to expand the size of his body, especially since he can literally inflate to giant proportions. For his Durance, let's look at his childhood with Ace and Sabo, where they took it upon themselves to beat the crap out of all the animals in the forest until they finally succeeded in defeating the apex predator who was a colossal tiger.<br /> <br /> As for the Pirate King, it would be in Luffy's own words.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't want to conquer anything, I think the person with the most freedom is the Pirate King.&quot;<br /> <br /> What could that mean? Well, what if he's a Changeling who is able to move and operate freely throughout Arcadia without being captured by the Gentry or becoming one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent points. His Kiths could be Skogsra and Lurker, since he shows a knack for dealing with beasts and lived as the adoptive son of mountain bandits. The problem is that Luffy has a horrible sense of direction and navigation in the manga and anime IIRC, which goes against the 8 Again that the Skogsra Kith gives to Survival and Stealth. Then again, a changeling that goes adventuring in the Hedge often but doesn't have a decent amount of survival skills is either going to die or need rescuing all the time, so I'll let it slide. His combat prowess and endurance are granted the Contracts Of Elasticity, Stone, some clauses of Mirror, lots of Fighting Styles and creative tactics.<br /> <br /> As for the Devil Fruit, they could have been left behind by a Gentry who achieved Wyrd Transcendence. Alternatively, the so called Sea Devil was a powerful hobgoblin whom even the Gentry couldn't destroy completely, so they had to rip it apart into countless pieces that were scattered across the Hedge, with each piece eventually regrowing inside the Thorns into a Devil Fruit. I'd say the Devil Fruit don't turn people into changelings: they are either acquired by Gentry somehow and a captive mortal eats it, or a mortal finds one in the Hedge and the resulting Contract is only activated after he is kidnapped and turned into a changeling. It is likely that eating or just possessing a Devil Fruit makes you a special target for Gentry and Huntsmen. In either case, the first Frailty the changeling develops is somehow themed after water or the sea. Given that one character cannot have multiple major templates in NWOD, the Devil Fruit only give their powers and curses to those of mortal or fae blood, excluding the Gentry. Tony Tony Chopper is a good example: he was a Hedge Beast or some other hobgoblin who had the luck of eating just the right Devil Fruit. Should a werewolf try to eat one of them, all that will happen is that he will spit out the chunk he bit and wash his tongue. I'd say the Devil Fruit even regenerate until eaten by a mortal or half-fae, and send out waves of Glamour that guarantee they will always be found.<br /> <br /> Lastly, your suggestion of what being a Pirate King means to Luffy is suitably long term and epic.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the suggestions!<br /> <br /> EDIT: On second thought, I don't remember Luffy being very skilled or interested in thievery. Skogsra + Earthbones probably fits better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-15-2015, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T22:00:54-07:00","id":701663,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say Luffy has a poor direction sense. He just loves to explore and see what comes of it, case and point he specifically wanted to go to the most dangerous islands in the New World.<br /> <br /> Zoro, on the other hand.... He gets lost following a bird that always faces south!<br /> <br /> Oh, and you're welcome. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-15-2015, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:33:49-07:00","id":934056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=524262#post524262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I will never step foot in Australia as long as I live! Raining a carpet of spiders gets you off my places I'd like to visit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hear what you are saying, but...the list of terrible ways you can die in Australia and the number of things waiting in the wild to screw you over is...well...Penny Arcade summed it up well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/27\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assets.penny-arcade.com/comics/20141027-0yxutFEz.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/27\" target=\"_blank\"> Underworld, Part One - Penny Arcade </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/27\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/27 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Videogaming-related online strip by Mike Krahulik and Jerry Holkins. Includes news and commentary. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/29/underworld-part-two\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assets.penny-arcade.com/comics/20141029-7PCLRP4e.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/29/underworld-part-two\" target=\"_blank\"> Underworld, Part Two - Penny Arcade </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/29/underworld-part-two\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/29/underworld-part-two </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Videogaming-related online strip by Mike Krahulik and Jerry Holkins. Includes news and commentary. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/31/underworld-part-three\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assets.penny-arcade.com/comics/20141031-OUYllV77.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/31/underworld-part-three\" target=\"_blank\"> Underworld, Part Three - Penny Arcade </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/31/underworld-part-three\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2014/10/31/underworld-part-three </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Videogaming-related online strip by Mike Krahulik and Jerry Holkins. Includes news and commentary. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just saying, you can take your pick of reasons not to go there. The Fae are well within their rights not to set foot on that nightmare rock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T14:25:08-07:00","id":934089,"title":"","content":"There was six of them, all rather young, and with little in common save for all of them being Windwings. It's been 4 years since they escaped from the School -- the nightmarish section of Arcadia filled with True Fae eager to experiment on whatever humans they could get their hands on. They thought that they had been forgotten by their captors, but the abduction of the youngest member of their group by a bunch of wolflike Huntsmen proved otherwise. Now they're risking their lives to go to Arcadia and get her back.<br /> <br /> (I swear, this is the last time I'm checking the Comic Con schedule while in a Changeling mood. The last thing I want is to be thinking of <i>this</i> train-wreck of a series again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T15:43:07-07:00","id":934141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=934056#post934056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hear what you are saying, but...the list of terrible ways you can die in Australia and the number of things waiting in the wild to screw you over is...well...Penny Arcade summed it up well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just saying, you can take your pick of reasons not to go there. The Fae are well within their rights not to set foot on that nightmare rock.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I forgot which comedian said this, but:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Australia's a nice place to visit, as long as you're in doors. But once you step outside, everything on the continent wants to kill you!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T17:22:03-07:00","id":939225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=934089#post934089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was six of them, all rather young, and with little in common save for all of them being Windwings. It's been 4 years since they escaped from the School -- the nightmarish section of Arcadia filled with True Fae eager to experiment on whatever humans they could get their hands on. They thought that they had been forgotten by their captors, but the abduction of the youngest member of their group by a bunch of wolflike Huntsmen proved otherwise. Now they're risking their lives to go to Arcadia and get her back.<br /> <br /> (I swear, this is the last time I'm checking the Comic Con schedule while in a Changeling mood. The last thing I want is to be thinking of <i>this</i> train-wreck of a series again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Maximum Ride kind of got...<i>incoherent.</i><br /> <br /> It always was, but it was the fun, silly kind until book four...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:23:22-07:00","id":990547,"title":"","content":"You know what would be an AMAZING Changeling story? Kill Six Billion Demons. I know it's very Exalted-y, but it's super changelingy too. The main character ends up dragged into a bizarre supernatural realm where she's physically and spiritually transformed at the whims of strange and capricious godlike beings. They even send a Fetch back to earth so people don't realize she's gone! You could have the demons as fae, hobs, or even either kind of ChroD demon: the way they use &quot;masks&quot; to give themselves identities could easily be adapted to Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T14:50:06-07:00","id":991535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=990547#post990547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what would be an AMAZING Changeling story? Kill Six Billion Demons. I know it's very Exalted-y, but it's super changelingy too. The main character ends up dragged into a bizarre supernatural realm where she's physically and spiritually transformed at the whims of strange and capricious godlike beings. They even send a Fetch back to earth so people don't realize she's gone! You could have the demons as fae, hobs, or even either kind of ChroD demon: the way they use &quot;masks&quot; to give themselves identities could easily be adapted to Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like it. it combines the best aspects of 1st edition and 2nd Edition Fae. Utterly alien and strange to the human senses, with time being fluid and unreal, but also tied to a narrative whose barebones elements can be understood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:03:42-07:00","id":991542,"title":"","content":"Any of the seven Demiurges would make a great keeper, too. The scene where they're having a meeting is pretty much a perfect illustration of how I'd imagine a gathering of True Fae playing out. And the hunters after Allison could easily be adapted into Privateers or Huntsmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:06:40-07:00","id":991544,"title":"","content":"What would the angels be? Changelings? Wisps of an abnormally powerful True Fae? Actors in their own right? Hobgoblins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:24:24-07:00","id":991585,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm, that's a tough one. It's hard not to just do them as GM angels. If I ever ran this or wrote it up, I'd be tempted to make Throne a Changeling/Demon crossover setting, an Arcadian realm that somehow has angels and Unchained present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:24:01-07:00","id":998292,"title":"","content":"I don't know why, but Slenderman as a rogue Scarecrow Minister High Wyrd, Low Clarity 2e Wizened Woodblood/Some Stealth Kith just makes a lot of sense to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-04-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:24:32-07:00","id":998293,"title":"","content":"I realize that's half-way to True Fae but Slendy as Changeling interests me more., largely becuase it means I can build him to be playable (unless he's Clarity 1 or 0)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-04-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:38:09-07:00","id":998303,"title":"","content":"Would the Danganronpa series be Durance-like enough? Or is there not enough transformation involved. I can only think of Mechumaru as someone who got transformed Changeling-style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:50:30-07:00","id":998625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=454157#post454157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had to read it twice to recognize it was Space Jam.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> Screaming... that's the only warning most people get before it happens. Massive explosions, unexplained natural disasters, or electronic devices over loading. Sometimes the screaming lasts for only a few seconds... other times it can go on for 10 whole minutes! You've heard the stories, people emitting death rays from their hands and blowing their foes to pieces in the blink of an eye. Warriors who gleam like the sun, or change their forms dramatically before your eyes. Many people die in the presence of these warriors, but sometimes they don't stay dead.<br /> <br /> The foes these warriors face have to be seen to be believed. From colossal weremonkeys, to albino lizards, giant midgets, clockwork teenagers, parasitic insects, elastic starfish, and even hairless cats!<br /> <br /> The land resembles our own Earth to a certain degree, but those who know of its existence refer to it simply as The Dragon World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Ball?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Give before you take, or I'll hit you with a rake&quot; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">~ Socrates</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5638-kaizer-gibby","name":"Kaizer Gibby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5638_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T05:18:12-07:00","id":998705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaizer Gibby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/19242-fae-ify-it?p=998625#post998625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Ball?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm thinking the Fae who run the realm may be the wish granting dragons summoned by a full set of Dragon Balls. The reason why they're so grumpy all the time is because they become physically vulnerable as long as they're granting wishes, and they want to get it over with quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-05-2016, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:25:13-07:00","id":998974,"title":"","content":"In 1790, in Tarry Town, New York, there was a school teacher named Ichabod Crane. Tall, lean, and lanky, he looked like a goofy scarecrow, he is resented and ostracized by most of the town folk for being an outsider. None the less, a favorite of the town ladies. One day, he falls in love with eighteen year old, Katrina Van Tassel, who is a daughter of the wealthy Baltus Van Tassel. Unfortunately, she is also courted by Abraham &quot;Brom Bones&quot; Van Blunt, the a rowdy and a bully, but popular the towns people for &quot;being one of them.&quot; Blunt first tries to drive Crane away by playing cruel pranks on him and spreading the rumor that Crane wants to marry Katrina to get a hold of the Van Tassel's wealth. Much to Blunt's frustration, Katrina is attracted more to the cultured and educated Ichabod Crane. One day, a stranger payed a visit to Blunt. If he can lead Ichabod Crane to Sleepy Hollow, Crane will be never be seen again. Brunt tells Crane that Baltus Van Tassel want to talk to Crane about marrying his daughter. Along the way, he passes through sleepy hollow, where a True Fae, the headless horseman, snatches him up, and Ichabod is never seen in the two again. Afterward, through the coercion of the towns people and the commands of her father, Katrina Van Tassel marries Abraham Blunt. Blunt eventually meets Washington Irving and tells him a mudslinging version of what what happened to Ichabod Crane (<i>Which Became the Tale of Sleepy Hollow)</i> to ruin Ichabod Crane's reputation. Ironically, Blunt eventually grows tired of her and gives her to the Headless Horseman, too.<br /> <br /> Over a century later, (in the year 1910) , two darklings, one male and one female come out of the hedge gate to Sleepy Hollow. They join the Autumn Court with the male eventually joining the Scarecrow Ministry and becomes one of its most infamous members. The tale he most often uses is that of <i>Sleepy Hollow.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:16:17-08:00","id":1008167,"title":"","content":"The webseries <i>Ever After High</i> is pretty Changeling. Its setting is literally dependent on everyone fulfilling their preordained roles, but at the same time it's a setting unto itself involving new relationships and plotlines between &quot;fairytale characters&quot; (i.e, those who inherited the actual <i>original</i> character's title/mantle/powers).<br /> <br /> And unlike every shitty attempt to cash in on fairytales by criticizing them (looking at <i>you</i>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maleficent_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Stromberg</a>) it doesn't butcher their plots out of political correctness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T17:46:47-08:00","id":1015913,"title":"","content":"No one seems to question the seemingly closed factory at the corner of town, the one with the tall smokestacks and iron gates. Parents sometimes recall a time in their lucid waking moments when the factory was open, and from it delivered delicious treats all over. But one day, posters appear over a town telling of great prizes, sweets, and golden tickets hidden in bars of chocolate. Through twists of fate, these tickets find their way into the hands of children, each spoiled beyond compare, and one pure and sweet child, just as sweet as the chocolate the golden tickets are hidden with. And when these children along with parents enter the factory, they meet the owner. Eccentric and oddly grim, he seemingly watches by in useless rapture as each child receives a judgement worthy of their vice, whilst his factory is populated by others who have been press-ganged into service with the temptation of more chocolate. Changed, twisted, and shrunk, these children are then released or kept according to his whimsy. But that 1 child who proved innocent to him is special. Oh yes, special indeed; the child to replace him when he is gone. Taught his special candymaking ways, the child becomes just like the owner, only to send golden tickets out again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12704-alloy-elf","name":"Alloy Elf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T01:10:01-08:00","id":1016022,"title":"","content":"These have been used before, but I couldn't help but put out my own interpretations. They're not entirely subtle though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your family has been murdered by something you cannot understand, and one being takes the credit. She tells you that you can get them back, indeed, that you can leave happy, if you play a game with her to stave off boredom. Simply explain to her how everyone died in a way that denies magic, and she'll even run you through how they could have died at least. However, she isn't showing you <i>exactly</i> what happened. After all this is just how they <i>could</i> have died. Everything in the gameboard she provides is magic - your grandfather was a magician, his elderly cook is possessed by your opponent's teacher, his servants are all magic themselves, and every hour sacrifices are made. Worse, even if you manage to get through one game with plausible deniability of magic, it isn't enough to end the games, and each gameboard is different. The pieces are the same, but the deaths are different and in different orders. Sometimes victims live when they otherwise died, and logic just doesn't work when your opponent is able to set down truths about what happened outside of the magic.<br /> <br /> The only way to win is to understand how the other side works...and even if you do, by that point you're practically ready to start hosting your own games. Would you even want to leave once you've discovered how the other side feels with these endless games?<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> He is a man. An impossible man, charming, intelligent, able to go anywhere within his realm and defeat the monsters within. Out of everyone within, he has chosen <i>you</i> to come along, his companion, to help him with his adventures, be rescued by him and ask him questions he will solve. He can pull anything out of his pockets, has a trunk that is massive within and inconspicuous without, and with it he can take you anywhere; he simply can't stop traveling to new places. Even when he would be defeated, he gets back onto his feet, remaking himself in all ways to be better than before. You and he are eternally young as you travel together, in this marvelous realm with this marvelous man.<br /> <br /> ...only, people seem to die where-ever he goes. Not you, <i>never</i> you, and the places you visit are always populated, but people have died in your arms. Sometimes you're changed. He makes sure you're changed back, perhaps with a few benefits left, but it's clear that there is danger. There are these strange rules, too, rules you need to remember if you don't want to annoy him and help him. Rules about time and this and that. He never explains things either...and when he gets angry, there are horrible consequences. It's rare the monsters don't make him angry. It should scare you when he is, but the joy of being rescued puts end to that...usually.<br /> <br /> You've also found clues, in his trunk, about him having other companions with him. He never talks about them, never tells you about them when asked. You don't even know his name, just a title that acts as one. You're sure things will never end...but you have to wonder, what will happen when they do? Will you be back at home, which he assures you is still there, even when you both never seem to end up in the right place when you want to visit it? Who are his people, the ones he says he ran away from? And why is he so scared of them, with their courts and politics, when he is so much better and freer than them?<br /> <br /> Are you entirely safe with this man?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T08:40:46-08:00","id":1029610,"title":"","content":"He doesn't know what's going on. One minute, it's his girlfriend's birthday- the next, this undead horde of...<i>abominations</i> is overrunning everything.<br /> Some of them look disconcertingly like his classmates.<br /> And that's not even the weirdest thing. His girlfriend has always been colourful, but now actual honest-to-God rainbows appear in her wake. (Or is it his perspective that's changed, not her?) Even while she's cutting up these monsters, so calmly it's like she's fought them a million times before. And that guy who teaches her karate after school is spouting something about 'realms colliding' and monsters spilling into earth.<br /> For the millionth time, he wishes he had a <i>normal</i> body to fight these guys with.<br /> Because this decaying-flesh-puppet crap is getting old <i>fast</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T21:40:44-08:00","id":1035619,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6gpb_dEqff0\" target=\"_blank\">This game looks promising.</a> <br /> <br /> &quot;The staff are murderers here. The guests are victims. But they are all controlled- dominated- by the masks they wear.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T18:24:17-07:00","id":1063067,"title":"","content":"I am astounded, in the best possible way, that this thread is still going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T18:25:48-07:00","id":1064110,"title":"","content":"He cannot move, he cannot speak, he cannot even think, not really. All he can do is watch as his keepers walk around this mansion, watch as weapons float through the air dragging him with them. He dies by the hands of each keeper over and over, in each room over, and by each eapon over and over. The rope, the revolver, the leadpipe... he dies in the ballroom and watches as Mrs. White cleans his blood stains off the floor. He watches as Professor Plum runs into the secret passageway as he lies bleeding to death on the conservatory floor.<br /> <br /> He hopes that someday his Keepers will figure out which one of them really killed him. He hope they will get a Clue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:24:40-07:00","id":1067637,"title":"","content":"*here are two possible perspectives on one conversion*<br /> <br /> You had a small talent, something special about you that science couldn't explain. Maybe you could hear missing objects calling out to you, maybe you could make fire move slightly, or maybe you just got headaches and nausea around certain people and places. Heck, you might have just been something natural, but strange like a contortionist. Whatever you could do, it wasn't enough to save you from them. Their recovery team always gets their quarry. They gave you a number and performed endless experiments on you and your powers. They've cut you open more times than you can remember, fed you the strangest substances just to record your reaction and, if you had the right powers, made you kill hundreds one by one. They will never let you go, for freaks like you are a danger to normal society, the ones they protect.<br /> <br /> And you thought being put on death row was going to be the worst thing that happened to you. But a few days with the Foundation have left you wishing you'd taken the injection instead. There's no way you should have survived this much physical and mental pain. It's been only luck and laziness on their part that allowed you to survive so long. Through so many experiments and procedures. You'll always wince at the word Montauk. They said the program would only last a month, but at night, you have dreams of procedures you don't remember. Far more experiments than even the Foundation could perform in a single month. Who knows how long you've been in here? Only the O-5s can tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:25:33-07:00","id":1068096,"title":"","content":"<u><b><i>Here's a Berserk conversion!</i></b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Idea of Evil:</b> not all ideas are good ones, and some in particular are especially detrimental to society. The Idea of Evil is an ancient, primordial Fey from the dawn of mankind's earliest existence. It claims to have been granted life by humanity's inability to accept the chaos of the world. Bad things didn't just happen for no reason, there had to be a cause. This philosophy gave birth to the beings we know now. It's soul existence revolves around giving humans a reason for their suffering. It has been watching our world, manipulating the laws of causality with the skillful hand of a god. It orchestrates events that span across generations, all to set the pieces in place for tragedy and wickedness to plague our lives.<br /> <br /> But as powerful as this thing is, it does not operate alone. Sometimes it finds a particular mortal that it takes a liking to, somebody who has the potential to advance its plans on earth. When it finds such a human, it singles them out, bestowing them with a hedge spun relic that binds them into a contract of servitude. Once received, The Idea of Evil visits upon them a tragedy of such proportion, that they have no choice but to sacrifice their heart in order to survive. That is when they change, becoming apostles of evil and it sends them loose upon mankind to work its will. They think their transformation has freed them, that they no longer need to fear The Idea of Evil's influence. They are wrong; they haven't cast off the shackles of Fate, they've only been made aware of them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-25-2017, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}